Variables
  ok      the Local scope lists the level-01 items of WORKING-STORAGE
  ok      alphanumeric items show their text
  ok      values reflect the statements executed so far
  BUG?    changing a numeric item stores the number, right-justified
            -> program output: "N=4200 NAME=ALICE   \n"
  ok      changing an alphanumeric item affects the rest of the execution
  BUG?    numeric DISPLAY items show a number, not their raw storage
            -> N shows "\"0005\""
  BUG?    signed decimal items show their sign and decimal point
            -> S (-12.5) shows "\"0125p\""
  BUG?    binary (COMP) items show their numeric value
            -> C (77) shows "\"\\000\\000\\000M\""
  BUG?    items are typed after their COBOL category
            -> N is typed group, NAME is typed group
  BUG?    group items expand into their subordinate items
            -> REC cannot be expanded (shows "\"042ABCD\"")
  BUG?    tables expand into their elements
            -> TBL cannot be expanded (shows "\"000700\"")
